{"name":"Clockwork Orange","hex":"#e07630","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Clockwork Orange","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Nickname for Netherlands national football team"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Clockwork_Orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"A Clockwork Orange (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"A Clockwork Orange is a novel by the English writer Anthony Burgess, published on 17 March 1962. It is set in a near-future society that has a youth subculture of extreme violence. The teenage protagonist, Alex, narrates his violent exploits and his experiences with state authorities intent on reforming him. The book is partially written in a Russian-influenced argot called \"Nadsat\", which takes its name from the Russian suffix that is equivalent to '-teen' in English. According to Burgess, the novel was a jeu d'esprit written in just three weeks."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/23/Clockwork_orange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Clockwork_Orange_(novel)"},{"title":"A Clockwork Orange (film)","blocks":[{"text":"A Clockwork Orange is a 1971 dystopian crime film written, produced, and directed by Stanley Kubrick. It is based on Anthony Burgess's 1962 novel. The film employs disturbing and violent themes to comment on psychiatry, juvenile delinquency, youth gangs, and broader social, political, and economic issues in a dystopian near-future Britain."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/73/A_Clockwork_Orange_%281971%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Clockwork_Orange_(film)"},{"title":"Clockwork Orange (plot)","blocks":[{"text":"Clockwork Orange was a secret British security services project alleged to have involved a right-wing smear campaign against British politicians from 1974 to 1975. The black propaganda led Prime Minister Harold Wilson to fear that the security services were preparing a coup d'état. The operation takes its name from A Clockwork Orange, a 1971 Stanley Kubrick film based on Anthony Burgess' 1962 novel of the same name."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clockwork_Orange_(plot)"},{"title":"Clockwork","blocks":[{"text":"Clockwork is the inner workings of either clocks and watches or other mechanical devices that work similarly, using a series of gears driven by a spring or a weight."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Prim_clockwork.jpg/330px-Prim_clockwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clockwork"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Malcolm_McDowell_Clockwork_Orange.png/500px-Malcolm_McDowell_Clockwork_Orange.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Malcolm_McDowell_Clockwork_Orange.png/500px-Malcolm_McDowell_Clockwork_Orange.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alex DeLarge in Kubrick's dystopian film A Clockwork Orange (1971)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMalcolm_McDowell_Clockwork_Orange.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Alex_and_his_droogies.jpg/500px-Alex_and_his_droogies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Alex_and_his_droogies.jpg/500px-Alex_and_his_droogies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vanessa Claire Smith, Sterling Wolfe, Michael Holmes, and Ricky Coates in Brad Mays' multi-media stage production of A Clockwork Orange, 2003, Los Angeles. (photo: Peter Zuehlke)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlex_and_his_droogies.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/A_Clockwork_Orange_-_the_treatment.jpg/330px-A_Clockwork_Orange_-_the_treatment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/A_Clockwork_Orange_-_the_treatment.jpg/330px-A_Clockwork_Orange_-_the_treatment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vanessa Claire Smith in Brad Mays' multi-media stage production of A Clockwork Orange, 2003, Los Angeles. (photo: Peter Zuehlke)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Clockwork_Orange_-_the_treatment.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Stanley_Kubrick_The_Exhibition_-_LACMA_-_A_Clockwork_Orange_-_Korova_Milk_Bar_%288998526527%29.jpg/500px-Stanley_Kubrick_The_Exhibition_-_LACMA_-_A_Clockwork_Orange_-_Korova_Milk_Bar_%288998526527%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Stanley_Kubrick_The_Exhibition_-_LACMA_-_A_Clockwork_Orange_-_Korova_Milk_Bar_%288998526527%29.jpg/1280px-Stanley_Kubrick_The_Exhibition_-_LACMA_-_A_Clockwork_Orange_-_Korova_Milk_Bar_%288998526527%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Stanley_Kubrick_The_Exhibition_-_LACMA_-_A_Clockwork_Orange_-_Korova_Milk_Bar_%288998526527%29.jpg/500px-Stanley_Kubrick_The_Exhibition_-_LACMA_-_A_Clockwork_Orange_-_Korova_Milk_Bar_%288998526527%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Human furniture from the Korova milk bar, where the \"milk-plus\" was served","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStanley_Kubrick_The_Exhibition_-_LACMA_-_A_Clockwork_Orange_-_Korova_Milk_Bar_(8998526527).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Lu